1. d4 d5 2. c4 e6 3. g3 c6 4. Bg2 Nf6 5. Nf3 Nbd7 6. O-O Bd6 7. Nc3 b6 8. e4
Nxe4 9. Nxe4 dxe4 10. Ng5 Nf6 11. Nxe4 Nxe4 12. Bxe4 Bb7 13. Qa4 Qc7 14. c5 $1
Be7 ({Black could hardly have done any worse by accepting the sacrifice:} 14...
bxc5 15. dxc5 Bxc5 {White gets his B to f4 and his rooks to d1 and c1
dominating the board, as in the game.}) 15. Bf4 Qd7 16. Rac1 O-O 17. Rfd1 b5
18. Qc2 h6 19. Qe2 g5 20. Be5 f5 ({If} 20... f6 {then} 21. Qh5 $1) 21. Bc2 Kh7
22. Rd3 a5 23. Re3 a4 24. b4 Rae8 25. Qh5 Bf6 26. Rce1 Bxe5 27. Rxe5 Re7 28. g4
Qe8 29. Qh3 Kg7 ({If} 29... Bc8 {White wins by} 30. gxf5 {just the same.}) 30.
gxf5 Bc8 31. fxe6 Rf6 32. Rxg5+ $1 Kf8 33. Rf5 Qg6+ 34. Qg3 Qxg3+ 35. fxg3 {
Source: Birmingham Daily Post, 8 January 1959 - BH Wood column} 1-0

