{Practically every congress has its stalemate incident. In this section there
occurred a stalemate plus legal (or rather illegal) fracas. In the diagrammed
position Black failed to observe that he was in check and played 1...Qf1+. The
tournament con­troller, Mr. Glyde, was called to the board and, since Black
could make a legal move with his Queen, he ruled that he must do so. Play went:
} 1... Qe4 2. Rb6 Qxc2 $4 3. Rxh6+ $1 {forcing a draw by stalemate. Vaguely we
discern a moral here. Source: BCM, February 1959, p39} 1/2-1/2

